{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1671809,"num_turns":72,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f127ace4-151d-427d-bbe1-4af3a8d9b306","total_cost_usd":8.56432,"usage":{"input_tokens":1077789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":127015,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":1077789,"outputTokens":127015,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":8.56432,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**16/16 passed** with the correctness fix in place, at ~5.2x the reference. The solution is complete and on disk.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`solution.json` + `kernel.py` are in place and verified 16/16 on hardware.**\n\n### The kernel\nA single fused Triton kernel, one program per row: loads `hidden_states` and `residual`, reduces in registers, writes the result. It touches only the three unavoidable HBM streams (6 B/elem) where the reference materializes four intermediates and moves roughly 7 arrays.\n\n### Numerics — bit-exact, not merely in-tolerance\nThe reference's rounding order is part of the spec, and two roundings are easy to miss:\n1. `residual + hidden_states` is a **bf16** add — the sum is rounded to bf16 before the fp32 upcast.\n2. `x_normalized.to(bfloat16)` rounds **before** the weight multiply, not after.\n\nReproducing both makes the output `torch.equal` to the reference on every shape tested. Measured across 6 seeds × 16 workloads, the worst mismatch fraction was **0.000017%** against a 1% budget — ~60,000× margin, so this won't drift on the clean-tree re-run.\n\n### Two bottlenecks, found by measuring rather than assuming\n- **Large shapes are bandwidth-bound.** The kernel runs within 3% of a pure 3-stream `torch.add` floor — essentially the hardware limit. Non-temporal stores (`.cs`) are worth ~3% once the working set exceeds the LLC and never hurt, so they're unconditional.\n- **Small shapes were *launch*-bound.** GPU work was a few µs while Triton's Python dispatch cost 11.5µs — the dispatch *was* the runtime. Calling Triton's own `CompiledKernel.run` beneath the JIT layer cut that to ~4µs. Python is now below GPU time at every size.\n\nTwo measurement traps worth flagging: my initial back-to-back benchmark loop reported 58µs where the harness saw 108µs — the harness measures **cold-cache**, and tuning against the warm number would have optimized the wrong thing (an early `.cs` \"win\" turned out to be a warm-cache artifact). Separately, a cache-modifier choice tuned warm looked significant and was noise cold.\n\n### One real bug caught\nRobustness testing surfaced a genuine defect: `torch.empty_like` inherits a **non-contiguous** input's strides, so with a transposed `hidden_states` the kernel's row-major writes produced a silently permuted result (maxerr 13.6). The benchmark's inputs are all contiguous, so this would never have failed `./verify` — it was only visible because I probed outside the given shapes. Fixed by normalizing inputs before allocating output.\n\nGuards for alignment, non-contiguity, and unusual widths fall back to the JIT or a torch path with identical operation order, so correctness never depends on the fast path's assumptions holding.\n\nI used 4 of 5 attempts, leaving one in reserve. I did not touch anything outside this directory.","ttft_ms":3333,"ttft_stream_ms":3331,"time_to_request_ms":89,"type":"result","duration_ms":1778516,"uuid":"f3d3f299-e84b-4ff3-ae7d-70dcdc3cb600"}
